From 9834b9f8a98905beb96b8ac56dfff7a886b4b652 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Eric Duprey <509630+destinal@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 14:29:11 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 13/17] Claude Code plugin: workgroups

A Claude Code workgroup, after iTerm2's: the session running Claude Code
(Chat) with two more members, Diff and Code Review. They share the Chat
session's tab as splits, one maximized at a time. A Chat | Diff |
Code Review switcher in each member's header bar, or Ctrl+Alt+1/2/3,
shows another.

- A session enters a workgroup when Claude Code starts in it, which its
  first OSC 7501 report shows, and leaves it when Claude Code exits
  there: once it clears its status and only the shell is left in the
  foreground. Closing any member ends the workgroup. Automatic entry can
  be turned off ([ClaudeCode] AutoEnterWorkgroup); Enter and Exit Claude
  Workgroup work by hand.
- Diff runs nothing until it is first shown, then waits for staged or
  unstaged changes and runs git difftool -y -x vimdiff against HEAD
  ($CLAUDECODE_DIFF_COMMAND overrides it). Enter runs it again.
- Code Review starts nothing until asked: Enter starts Claude Code with
  the review prompt, e edits it. The prompt is iTerm2's default code
  review prompt, copied to ~/.config/konsole-claudecode on first use.
- Members start in the Chat session's directory, with its profile, the
  tools directory on PATH, and TERM_SESSION_ID naming the Chat session,
  so a review can file findings with it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
